==== Reviewer note: live-environment contamination during the M2b-cycle2 review run ====
The full milestone Validation command (run once, in background, as required) exited 1: the
model-swap-proof.sh Step 4 (persistence after 600s idle) reported /api/ps == ["nemotron3:33b"]
instead of the expected ["qwen3.6:27b"]. Steps 1-3 (swap A->B, chat reply, keep_alive -1 after
the reply) all PASSED. ops/scripts/e2e-tailnet-proof.sh, server bun test/typecheck/entry-smoke,
ops bun test/verify-ops-install, and the mobile typecheck/unit tests/lint/smoke:runtime/
model-list-proof all PASSED before this point. Because model-swap-proof.sh failed, the `&&` chain
stopped there: model-failed-load-proof.sh and the expo export never ran as part of that single
command.

Investigation (server/src/models/manager.ts's `ollama serve` stdout, /private/tmp/ollama.log,
found via `lsof -a -p <ollama pid> -d 1 -Fn`): during the 600s idle window the log shows repeated
POST /api/chat and /api/generate calls (e.g. 21:30:02, 21:38:17, 21:38:51, 21:39:23) that the
swap-proof script itself never issues in its idle loop (it only polls GET /api/ps). This traffic,
and further /api/chat calls continuing after the run finished (21:40:46, 21:41:22, 21:41:38) with
GET /api/tags and /api/ps every 10-20s in between, show a separate, still-active client using this
Mac's Ollama directly (bypassing this server) throughout and after the review's live run, contrary
to "run nothing else against the Mac while it runs." A direct check confirmed nemotron3:33b was
still resident afterward even though the proof's own cleanup trap had restored devstral:24b
moments earlier and the trap ran to completion.

This is judged to be environmental contamination by an unrelated concurrent process, not a
regression from the M2b-C1 correction under review: the correction only reorders when
ModelManager.unload() claims `this.operation`, and touches nothing about OllamaClient.load's
keep_alive value, runLoad, or residency/idle persistence. Steps 1-3 (using the corrected code)
reproduced cycle 1's clean result before the external interference appeared.

Re-ran mobile/scripts/model-failed-load-proof.sh alone afterward (fresh, live, ~40s): PASSED
cleanly, independently reconfirming M2-AC5 against the corrected code (see log appended above,
timestamped 20:42:55 UTC). Did not re-attempt the 600s swap-proof a second time given ongoing,
still-observed unrelated Ollama traffic at the time (would likely be re-contaminated) and time
budget; M2-AC2/AC3 are graded on Steps 1-3 of today's run, cycle 1's full clean live proof of the
same steps (M2b-T3a-verifier.log, unaffected by this cycle's diff), and this cycle's new unit
tests, which directly assert that a completed unload() sweep still leaves `state.resident` null.

Mac restored by hand afterward to only devstral:24b resident, keep_alive -1 (unloaded
nemotron3:33b with keep_alive:0, then loaded devstral:24b with keep_alive:-1 via /api/generate,
confirmed via /api/ps). This may not hold if the unrelated external process continues to use the
Mac's Ollama after this review ends.
